1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,720
I’m sure we all have childhood memories – what we did at school, the food we ate, the games we played.
我相信每个人都有属于自己的童年回忆——上学时的趣事、吃过的美食、玩过的游戏。

2
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:12,880
But perhaps the most vivid recollections are those of the toys we played with.
但或许最鲜活的记忆，是那些陪伴我们成长的玩具。

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:21,680
There were many gadgets that may seem unsophisticated now but were the must-have items in the playground back in the day.
有许多小玩意儿如今看来可能显得简陋，但在当年的操场上，它们可是人手必备的热门单品。

4
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:27,730
Now it seems that our passion for nostalgia means some of them are making a comeback.
而现在，人们对怀旧情怀的热衷，让其中一些玩具正重新流行起来。

5
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:36,370
One of my favourites was the Nintendo Game Boy, which returned to the shops last year, 30 years after it was first released.
我最喜欢的玩具之一就是任天堂的Game Boy掌上游戏机。这款产品在发布30年后，于去年重返市场。

6
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:45,850
This handheld console has had some modifications, but still offers a simple gaming experience and a trip down memory lane!
它的掌机外观做了些许改良，但依旧能带来简单纯粹的游戏体验，让人重温往昔时光！

7
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:50,520
If the Game Boy wasn’t from your era, how about the Tamagotchi?
如果Game Boy不属于你的童年时代，那电子宠物鸡呢？

8
00:00:50,520 --> 00:01:01,790
This egg-shaped, plastic pet that its owner had to keep ‘alive’ with constant care and attention - was the must-have item not long after its launch in 1996.
这款鸡蛋形状的塑料宠物玩具需要玩家必须悉心照料才能让它“存活”下去，于1996年推出后不久就成了爆款。

9
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:09,880
These sometimes annoying ‘creatures’ were such a distraction in the classroom, they often got banned from school.
这些有时会惹人烦的“小家伙”在教室分散学生们的注意力，因此常常被学校禁止带入。

10
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:22,270
But now, childlike adults can relive their wasted youth because Japanese manufacturer Bandai will soon release an all-colour, new-and-improved version of the classic toy.
但如今，童心未泯的成年人可以重拾逝去的青春了——日本制造商万代即将推出这款经典玩具的全新彩色升级版。

11
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:31,530
Its maker says it’s evolved from a pet into more of a character, and can inhabit different lands, as well as get married and breed.
制造商表示，新款电子宠物鸡不再只是一个宠物，更像是一个角色，它可以居住在不同的场景中，还能结婚生子。

12
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:35,480
So what’s driving this demand for retro goods?
那么，是什么催生了人们对复古商品的需求呢？

13
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:44,140
Retail Analyst for Mintel, Chana Baram, told the BBC people are searching for comfort in 'the good old days'.
英敏特零售分析师钱娜·巴拉姆向英国广播公司表示，人们正从“往昔的美好时光”中寻求慰藉。

14
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:56,250
Certainly, playing with an old toy brings back memories of our formative years and gives us a feel-good factor, but it’s also something brands and marketing companies want to cash in on.
诚然，把玩旧玩具能唤起我们成长时期的回忆，带来愉悦的心情，但这也是各大品牌和营销公司想要从中牟利的商机。

15
00:01:56,250 --> 00:02:00,850
Retro toys are also something we could cash in on too.
我们普通人也可以从复古玩具中获益。

16
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:06,580
In the darkest corners of many attics and spare rooms lie the toys of Christmas past.
许多家庭的阁楼和闲置房间的角落里，都藏着当年圣诞节收到的玩具。

17
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:13,080
And those once much-loved and played with presents may now have a value beyond nostalgia.
这些曾经备受喜爱的礼物，如今的价值或许早已超越了怀旧本身。

18
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:22,700
Toyologist Peter Jenkinson told the BBC that any number of "toys that we all played with as kids are now worth more than a few quid".
玩具专家彼得·詹金森向英国广播公司透露，“我们小时候玩过的很多玩具，现在都价值不菲”。

19
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:31,730
He suggests there’s a real collectors' market for certain old board games, Star Wars characters, Sindy dolls and Lego sets.
他指出，一些老式棋盘游戏、星球大战人物模型、仙蒂娃娃和乐高套装，在收藏市场上十分走俏。

20
00:02:31,730 --> 00:02:40,180
However, if you own something like this, it may be just too precious to sell, and part with the connection to your childhood.
不过，如果你也珍藏着这样的玩具，它或许会因为承载着童年的回忆而太过珍贵，让你舍不得出售，不愿割舍这份与童年的联结。
